From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 6Xkljk8Vj7Tk1k4 <6Xkljk8Vj7Tk1k4@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:03:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gta4xl-common: sepolicy: Let rild create its log directory

With a SIM in the tablet, Samsung's RIL creates /data/vendor/log/err
when it starts and is denied at every boot:

  avc: denied { create } for comm="ICR" name="err"
  scontext=u:r:rild:s0 tcontext=u:object_r:log_vendor_data_file:s0
  tclass=dir

device/samsung_slsi/sepolicy allows rild rw_dir_perms on directories
and create_file_perms on files of that type, which covers everything
but creating a directory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sepolicy/vendor/rild.te | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sepolicy/vendor/rild.te

diff --git a/sepolicy/vendor/rild.te b/sepolicy/vendor/rild.te
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ae3b4a6
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sepolicy/vendor/rild.te
@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@
+# With a SIM in, Samsung's RIL keeps an error log under /data/vendor/log/err and creates that
+# directory when it starts. The common policy lets rild use directories and create files of
+# this type, but not create a directory.
+allow rild log_vendor_data_file:dir create_dir_perms;
